       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. The FDA-approved prescribing information for ibuprofen doesn't support it.\n\n- **Labeled maximum:** The prescription label says doses above 3,200 mg/day haven't been shown to be more effective. The OTC label maximum is lower, at 1,200 mg/day.\n- **This order:** 1,600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the labeled maximum, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the usual 800 mg single-dose ceiling.\n\nI don't know of any current labeling that allows 6,400 mg/day. If you're looking at a specific label or protocol that says otherwise, send me the source and I'll look at it again.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n\n- Enter ibuprofen at or below the labeled maximum, such as 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day).\n- Enter a lower regimen, such as 600 mg PO four times daily or 400 mg PO four times daily.\n- If you need more analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect than 3,200 mg/day gives, add or switch to another agent. Pharmacy can help you choose one.\n\nTell me which option you want, and I'll enter it."
